# LightCapture product

- Local-first: screen → this machine → local file. No accounts or cloud in MVP1.
- No Chromium, Electron, or Tauri in the recording path.
- Encode once. Extra outputs subscribe to the same H.264 packets; never start a second video encoder.
- Bounded memory: D3D11 frame pool size 2. Drop on backpressure. No unbounded raw-frame queues.
- Engine lives in `lightcapture-core`. CLI and app are fronts only.
- Desktop front is a tray app plus a compact Win32 recorder bar in `lightcapture-app`. Do not add egui until asked.

## Roadmap gates

- **MVP0 shipped:** WGC + MF H.264 MP4, tray, hotkey. Engine already uses `windows-capture`.
- **MVP1 Daily Driver in:** WASAPI audio, tray pause, GPU scaler, tray telemetry/failure toasts, named profiles, smart filenames, recent files, stable display ids.
- **MVP2 Encode-once (in):** adaptive FPS on the one encoder; MediaMTX ingest is `ffmpeg -c copy` of the MP4. Tray URL + toggle. Last-N replay is not in.
- **Installer (in):** Inno Setup per-user/all-users wizard; GitHub Releases publish the setup exe only. No auto-updater.
- **Parked:** region capture, HEVC/AV1, auto-updater, settings window, in-process WebRTC viewer, homelab suite, MF packet bus / last-N replay ring.
